Invocation: `/skill:star-expt-digest [PLAN_NAME | <N>d | <YYYY-MM-DD> | all | ledger] [DESCRIPTION]`. This run's argument is substituted here at load time — `$ARGUMENTS` — and nothing between those backticks means none was given. This skill runs in its own context (`context: fork`), so that substitution is the only place the argument appears: there is no user turn behind it to re-read, and taking an argument that is there as absent silently runs a different mode than the one asked for — with `ledger`, a different file. No argument resumes from the newest digest's `covers.through` and covers everything after it; a plan name (slug / numeric prefix / filename) covers that node's family with no time bound; `7d` or `2026-07-01` sets an explicit window; `all` covers the whole history and restarts the series; `ledger` writes a different artifact entirely — the combined table of which model wrote what at `wkdrs/digests/MODEL_LEDGER.md` (Step 8). Anything left after that is a description (conventions §7.12): in your own words, what this run is for. Prose that names no mode and resolves to no plan is description alone, not a missing argument — resume from the newest digest's `covers.through` as with no argument, and say so before writing anything. A lone token that parses as neither a window nor a plan is not a description; it stays the ambiguity this skill asks about. A description can steer what the digest highlights; it never widens or narrows the window the argument set.
